 "narrative": [
  "Of 4,338 customers who ever bought, 2,845 came back for a second order (65.58%), and 391 reached ten orders (9.01% of the top).",
  "The largest drop-off is at 'Returned for a 2nd order', losing 1,493 customers (34.42%). That is where an intervention has the most people to act on -- which is not the same as where it has the most value.",
  "Overlaying revenue makes that distinction concrete: customers who reach five or more orders are 26% of the base but 71% of revenue. Fixing the first-to-second-order step moves the most customers; keeping the deep repeaters protects the most money. A funnel chart alone would hide the second fact.",
  "This is a purchase-count funnel, not a web funnel: the dataset has no sessions or page views, so the steps are the ones the transactions actually support rather than the ones a template suggests."
